"7de7d614-76c9-5133-a4df-95f079467cb9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Inequality With No Constant Term Using the Sign Table Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "616d9703-bb2c-54e3-b0c7-e6b17aff594a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "616d9703-bb2c-54e3-b0c7-e6b17aff594a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277388} :answer-field/id #uuid "067b0b81-cbe9-5008-9a99-a684b973c7e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "735beae0-3134-5841-bd7e-e50c7dd12138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "735beae0-3134-5841-bd7e-e50c7dd12138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277390} :answer-field/id #uuid "761c0d1d-256e-595f-b75c-006bf51d24bf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e180884-f60a-5dfa-81f7-5572df2d3179" :question/math-academy-id "q-277162" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is $2{x}^{2}-10x\\le 0?$\n\n$x\\in [$\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-10x & \\le 0 \\\\ 2x(x-5) & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $2x(x-5)=0.$ The roots are $x=0$ and $x=5,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ $(0,5),$ and $(5,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $(0,5)$ | $(5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $2x(x-5)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $2x(x-5)\\le 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $2x(x-5)$ is zero or negative.\n\nWe see that the expression is negative on the interval $(0,5).$ Also, we know that the expression equals $0$ at the points $x=0$ and $x=5.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $2{x}^{2}-10x\\le 0$ for all \n\n$$\nx\\in [0,5].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b23c4da-7a8d-5076-a4e9-8bcde40bc088" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Table of Signs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4164ceb-7866-5c18-a8a7-a04b6f3c5f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "−" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052321} {:answer/id #uuid "52935c97-3833-598c-bf26-ecd82e243017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52935c97-3833-598c-bf26-ecd82e243017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052322} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c07aa8f-a8aa-5cb9-8950-7f227bcd91fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164b7309-244b-5189-ba82-4a2a942ff073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "−" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052324} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc73bcc-8780-578a-95e3-acd551eac9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fc73bcc-8780-578a-95e3-acd551eac9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052325} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac2a043-39e6-53d0-b825-fa5ef153d6d6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491941b9-f74b-5ae6-ad61-50f92d4a4231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "−" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052327} {:answer/id #uuid "5700fa79-3046-58a3-ab3c-18395e2ec309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491941b9-f74b-5ae6-ad61-50f92d4a4231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "−" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052327} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de7539b-df42-5696-94df-5af24a041745" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03df1550-dcf6-5c97-ae0d-3b6f1f117ab2" :question/math-academy-id "q-277702" :question/problem "Choose the appropriate signs for the sign table shown below. \n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-11),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=-15.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =-15+11=(-),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ |  |  |\n\n- On the interval $(-11,0),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =-1+11=(+),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ | $+$ |  |\n\n- On the interval $(0,\\infty ),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =5+11=(+),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de7d614-76c9-5133-a4df-95f079467cb9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Inequality With No Constant Term Using the Sign Table Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a5de5db-af31-5967-803e-4dc8088c5057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277393} {:answer/id #uuid "2b124310-6681-5e10-95a8-905e4be80586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a5de5db-af31-5967-803e-4dc8088c5057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277393} :answer-field/id #uuid "919898ec-c611-5568-93fc-0136859b3ca5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94185306-df5d-5eb0-8a02-d727d74eaa56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94185306-df5d-5eb0-8a02-d727d74eaa56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277396} :answer-field/id #uuid "8360227f-0161-5e7f-aab4-f8afa3f58c95" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c46d992c-c35d-5326-ac4c-fadb922cc91c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c46d992c-c35d-5326-ac4c-fadb922cc91c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277398} :answer-field/id #uuid "e84cec04-2b17-5b21-b7a6-993c6524c52d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b04d22af-bc1b-5b2e-8220-05548278bd31" :question/math-academy-id "q-278299" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is ${x}^{2}+7x\\ge 0?$\n\n$x\\in (-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}\n$]\\cup [$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+7x & \\ge 0 \\\\ x(x+7) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $x(x+7)=0.$ The roots are $x=-7$ and $x=0,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,-7),$ $(-7,0),$ and $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-7)$ | $(-7,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x+7$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x(x+7)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(-)\\cdot (+)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x+7)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $x(x+7)$ is zero or positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-7)$ and $(0,\\infty ).$ Also, we know that the expression equals $0$ at the points $x=-7$ and $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}+7x\\ge 0$ for all \n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,-7]\\cup [0,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a186b166-928c-5bad-a996-3bdf6af419f5" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Inequality Using the Sign Table Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adf8fc50-be2d-51ac-b31d-2a69291ac707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adf8fc50-be2d-51ac-b31d-2a69291ac707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277401} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5964b6-afdc-5360-8e33-20d400f9fa8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277400} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52678296-4224-5234-89ba-314a358ae82b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52678296-4224-5234-89ba-314a358ae82b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277403} :answer-field/id #uuid "e17d06b0-32df-5aaa-bac4-7931d97ad304" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed64eec-bfd3-5aba-90ad-316e456605b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ed64eec-bfd3-5aba-90ad-316e456605b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277405} :answer-field/id #uuid "09a848c1-9267-541e-a5a5-b93b2849997b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc316b99-70b7-587c-92f7-20a14a37bd6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-278306" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is ${x}^{2}+4x+3>0?$\n\n$x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cup ($\n{{field-3}}\n$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & >0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+1) & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $(x+3)(x+1)=0.$ The roots are $x=-3$ and $x=-1,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,-3),$ $(-3,-1),$ and $(-1,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(-3,-1)$ | $(-1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+3$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $(x+3)(x+1)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $(x+3)(x+1)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $(x+3)(x+1)$ is positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(-1,\\infty ).$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}+4x+3>0$ for all \n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (-1,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b23c4da-7a8d-5076-a4e9-8bcde40bc088" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Table of Signs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7caf2ae-2a11-5646-b881-86fcc72743a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277408} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7d3685-a7c8-54c2-9042-f5d944efd3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7caf2ae-2a11-5646-b881-86fcc72743a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277408} :answer-field/id #uuid "880947f3-d69b-5a65-be9a-5513b726735a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277407} {:answer-